                <pb facs="0761" n="676" sameAs="frus:frus1919v02/pg676"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">817.00/2606: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Nicaragua</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Jefferson</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Acting Secretary of
                            State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Managua</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1919-06-25T14:00:00-05:45"><hi rendition="#italic">June 25, 1919,
                                2 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[<hi rendition="#italic">Received June 26,
                            3.11 a.m.</hi>]</dateline></opener>
                <p>Referring to my cable of June 9th, 11 a.m. Mr. Canton within the next 10 days
                    expects to arrive at Bluefields to assume duties.</p>
                <p>Now that matters have been placed in his hands, I do not believe that there will
                    be any difficulty in the prompt and satisfactory settlement of the pending
                    question including expulsion decree.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Jefferson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
